    "heading": "Warming Up With Ians Quick Grid",
    "body": "Happy Saturday, everyone! I hope you have a large cup of coffee ready because todays Pips puzzles are a total blast. I started the easy grid by looking at that lonely sum target of 5 in the top row at cell 0,1. Since there were not many dominoes that could fit there, I placed the 5-end of the [2,5] piece at 0,1 and tucked the 2-end into the empty spot at 1,1. It felt like a solid anchor to start the day.\n\nNext, I moved over to the bottom left where we had a target sum of 9 across three cells. I noticed the [4,4] domino was just begging to be used, so I placed it at 3,0 and 4,0. To finish off that sum of 9, I needed a 1 at 2,0. Luckily, I had the [0,1] domino left, which fit perfectly when I connected it to the empty spot at 2,1. The whole thing snapped together like a dream once I used the [3,5] and [0,4] pieces to satisfy the remaining targets on the right side.",
